## What this predicate means

**A `implemented-by` B** — B is a concrete realization of A (inverse of `implements`).  The author-side advertisement: "this specification has known implementations."

Specification memorials (interfaces, protocols, patterns) use `implemented-by:` to point at their working instances — useful for downstream consumers seeking concrete examples of the abstract contract.

